Venser has flash and bounces a SPELL, so he is a hard counter that leaves a 2/2 Wizard behind. Everything else in the deck exists to make that trigger happen again — blink him, copy him, double his trigger — until the table cannot resolve anything. And because he is a Wizard, the tribal payoffs that tap Wizards for value are all live at the same time.

# The commander
Venser, Shaper Savant :: flash, and his enters trigger returns a target spell OR permanent to its owner's hand. Hold four mana and he answers a wrath, a combo piece or a commander at instant speed.
Naban, Dean of Iteration :: if a WIZARD entering triggers an ability of a permanent you control, it triggers again. Venser is a Wizard, so every arrival bounces two things.
Panharmonicon :: the same doubling for any creature or artifact.
Roaming Throne :: name Wizard. A third doubler, on a ward {2} body.
Archmage of Echoes :: copies every Faerie or Wizard PERMANENT spell you cast. Casting Venser makes two Vensers and two bounces.

# Blinking him, over and over
Displacer Kitten :: every noncreature spell you cast blinks a permanent you control. Point it at Venser and each counterspell, each cantrip, each removal spell also bounces something of theirs. This is the deck's engine.
Conjurer's Closet :: a free blink every end step, forever.
Essence Flux :: one mana.
Displace :: two creatures at once, at instant speed.
Blur :: a blink and a card.
Planar Incision :: a blink that leaves a +1/+1 counter, and it works on artifacts too.
Dour Port-Mage :: bounces one of your own creatures every turn for {1}{U}, and draws whenever your creatures leave without dying.
Barrin, Tolarian Archmage :: bounces a creature or planeswalker on arrival, and draws at end step whenever a permanent went to your hand from the battlefield — which this deck does every single turn.
Aether Channeler :: three modes, all of which are fine, and all of which double under Naban.

# The Wizard engines
Azami, Lady of Scrolls :: tap any untapped Wizard to draw a card. On a board of five Wizards that is five cards a turn.
Patron Wizard :: tap a Wizard to tax every spell they cast. Alongside Azami it makes your board a soft counterspell wall.
Galecaster Colossus :: tap a Wizard to bounce any nonland permanent they control. With enough Wizards it is a one-sided board wipe every turn.
Sage of Fables :: every other Wizard arrives with a +1/+1 counter, and counters convert into cards.
Docent of Perfection :: a Wizard token per instant or sorcery, then it flips into an anthem that keeps making them.
Kindred Discovery :: name Wizard. A card for every Wizard that enters AND every one that attacks — and this deck flickers Wizards constantly.
Herald's Horn :: Wizards cost one less and it digs for them each upkeep.
Patchwork Banner :: an anthem plus fixing.
Psychosis Crawler :: each opponent loses a life for every card you draw. With Azami running that is lethal quickly.

# Interaction
Counterspell :: the clean two-mana answer.
Mana Drain :: counter, and the mana casts Venser at instant speed.
An Offer You Can't Refuse :: one mana for anything noncreature.
Glen Elendra Archmage :: a repeatable counterspell for noncreature spells, twice thanks to persist.
Glen Elendra Guardian :: flash, flies, and counters a noncreature spell while drawing them a card they do not need.
Pongify :: one mana, kills anything.
Rapid Hybridization :: the second copy.
Cyclonic Rift :: overloaded, the clear for a lethal Wizard attack.
Raise the Palisade :: name Wizard and every other creature at the table goes back to hand.
Cyclone Summoner :: cast from hand, it returns ALL permanents except Giants, Wizards and lands. Your board survives; nobody else's does.
Master of Waves :: protection from red, an anthem, and a pile of Elemental tokens scaled to your devotion.

# Card flow
Rhystic Study :: their turns pay for your instant-speed turns.
Mystic Remora :: the best card in the deck on turns one through four.
Archaeomancer :: returns an instant or sorcery on entry, and blinks for another every turn.
Quistis Trepe :: casts an instant or sorcery from ANY graveyard on entry, and blinks to do it again.
Emeritus of Ideation :: a 5/5 flier that also carries an Ancestral Recall.
Candlekeep Sage :: your commander draws a card whenever he enters OR leaves — so every blink is two cards.
Sapphire Medallion :: everything costs one less.
Mind Stone :: ramp early, a card later.

# What to keep in an opening hand
Keep mana and a cheap Wizard. The deck wants to be holding up four mana from turn four onwards, and Venser is only a counterspell if you can actually cast him at instant speed.
Cast Venser on THEIR turn whenever possible. Bouncing a spell off the stack is strictly better than bouncing a permanent, and holding him up costs you nothing because he is also your best blocker-answer.
Displacer Kitten :: prioritise her over any single Wizard. With Venser on the battlefield she turns every cheap blue spell in the deck into a two-for-one.
Naban, Dean of Iteration :: two mana, and he doubles the most important trigger in the deck. Play him before you start blinking, not after.
